    "bio": "A Representative from Texas; born in Los Angeles, Calif., September 19, 1947; attended public schools of Lockhart, Tex.; graduated, Kimball High School, Dallas, Tex., 1966; B.A., University of Texas, Austin, 1971; businessman; president and founder of manufacturing company; member, city council, Dallas, Tex., 1977-1981; delegate, Texas State Republican conventions, 1972-1982; elected as a Republican to the Ninety-eighth and to the four succeeding Congresses and served from January 3, 1983, until his resignation March 11, 1991; is a resident of Dallas, Tex.",
